G4250.def:
πρίν 
__1. as adv. of time, before, formerly (cl.; 3Ma.5:28 3Mac 6:4 3Mac 6:31)
__2. As conic. (cl.), before; 
__(a) after a positive sentence, with accusative and inf.: Matthieu 26:34, 75, Marc 14:72, Luc 22:61, Jean 4:49 8:58 (where D. om. γενέσθαι and π. becomes prep. with genitive; see Bl., § 69, 7) Jean 14:29, Actes 2:20" (LXX), WH, txt.; πρὶν ἤ (not such good Attic in this construction; see Bl., l.with), Matthieu 1:18 Marc 14:30, Actes 2:20, WH, mg., Actes 7:2; 
__(b) after a negative sentence, πρὶν ἤ: a. subjc. (before ἄν, M, Pr., 169), Luc 2:26; with optative, Actes 25:16.†

G4253.def:
πρό 
prep. with genitive, [in LXX chiefly for פָּנִים ;] 
before; 
__(a) of place: Actes 12:6, 14 14:13, Jacques 5:9; π. προσώπου (= Heb. פָּנִים, Deutéronome 3:18, Malachie 3:1, al.; Bl., § 40, 9), Matthieu 11:10, Marc 1:2, Luc 1:76 7:27 9:52 10:1, Actes 14:13; 
__(b) of time: Matthieu 8:29 24:38, Luc 11:38 21:12, Jean 11:55 13:1 17:24, Actes 5:36 21:38, 1 Corinthiens 2:7 4:5, Éphésiens 1:4, Colossiens 1:17, 2 Timothée 1:9 4:21, Tite 1:2, Hébreux 11:5, 1 Pierre 1:20, Ju 25; π. ἐτῶν δεκατεσσάρων, fourteen years ago, 2 Corinthiens 12:2; π. προσώπου (see supr.), Actes 13:24; with genitive of person(s), Matthieu 5:12, Jean 5:7 10:8, Romains 16:7, Galates 1:17; with genitive art. inf. (= πρίν; M, Pr., 100; Bl., § 69, 7), Matthieu 6:8 Luc 2:21 22:15, Jean 1:49 13:19 17:5, Actes 23:15, Galates 2:12 3:23; as in late writers (resembling a Latin idiom but indepen­dent of it; B1., § 40, 5; M, Pr., 100 f.; of. Am 2Ma.15:36, and for other exx., Soph., Lex., see word), πρὸ ἓξ ἡμέρας τοῦ πάσχα, on the sixth day before the Passover, Jean 12:1; 
__(with) of preference: π. πάντων, Jacques 5:12, 1 Pierre 4:8; 
__(d) in compos., 
__α with subst., of position before: προαύλιον, πρόδρομος; priority of rank or order, προπάτωρ; anticipation, πρό γνωσις, πρό νοια; 
__β with adj., intensity, πρόδηλος; 
__γ with verb., of place, προάγω, προβαίνω; of preference, προαιρέομαι.†

G4254.def:
προ-άγω 
[in LXX: 1 Rois 17:16 (נָגַשׁ), Wis.19:11, al. ;] 
__1. prop. trans., to lead on, lead forth or forward: with accusative of person(s), Actes 16:30 17:5; of bringing forth to trial, Actes 12:6 (WH, txt., προσάγ-); before ἐπί, with genitive of person(s), Actes 25:26. 
__2. Intrans. (Plat., Polyb., and later writers; see Bl., § 53, 1; MM, xxi); 
__(a) to lead the way, 1 Timothée 1:18 (R, mg.), hence, to go before, precede: Luc 18:39; opposite to ἀκολουθέω, Marc 11:9; before εἰς, Matthieu 14:22, Marc 6:45, 1 Timothée 5:24, Hébreux 7:18; with accusative of person(s), Matthieu 2:9 21:9, Marc 10:32; before εἰς, Matthieu 21:31 26:32 28:7, Marc 14:28 16:7; 
__(b) to go on, advance (Sir.20:27): 2Jn.9.†

G4291.def:
προ-ΐστημι 
[in LXX: 2 Rois 13:17, Proverbes 23:5 26:17, Ésaïe 43:24, Amos 6:10 (no proper Heb. equiv.), Dan LXX Bel 1:7, 1Ma.5:19, 4Ma.11:27 * ;] 
__1. trans. in fut., 1 aor., and mid. 1 aor., to put before, set over (Plat., al.). 
__2. Intrans., in pf., plpf., 2 aor. and mid. Pres. and impf.; 
__(a) to preside, rule, govern: Romains 12:8, 1 Timothée 5:17; with genitive, 1 Thessaloniciens 5:12, 1 Timothée 3:4-5 3:12; 
__(b) to direct, maintain: with genitive of thing(s), καλῶν ἔργων, Tite 3:8, 14 (on R, mg., profess honest occupations, see CGT, in l; Field, Notes, 223 f.).†
